    <item>
      <title>When a Uniswap V3 Vault Prices Its Own Shares at the Edge of Its Range</title>
      <link>https://yinhui1984.github.io/when-a-uniswap-v3-vault-prices-its-own-shares-at-the-edge-of-its-range/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2026 12:41:48 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://yinhui1984.github.io/when-a-uniswap-v3-vault-prices-its-own-shares-at-the-edge-of-its-range/</guid>
      <category domain="https://yinhui1984.github.io/categories/security/">Security</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;A Gelato G-UNI vault on Arrakis Finance priced its own shares off a Uniswap V3 position&amp;rsquo;s current-block valuation. Moderate price manipulation looked harmless — it wasn&amp;rsquo;t, once the price crossed the position&amp;rsquo;s own range boundary in one swap.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Term Finance: A DAO With 0.535 Tokens: How Someone Bought a Yearn Vault for 0.55 WETH</title>
      <link>https://yinhui1984.github.io/term-finance-a-dao-with-0.535-tokens-how-someone-bought-a-yearn-vault-for-0.55-weth/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 24 Aug 2026 09:59:52 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://yinhui1984.github.io/term-finance-a-dao-with-0.535-tokens-how-someone-bought-a-yearn-vault-for-0.55-weth/</guid>
      <category domain="https://yinhui1984.github.io/categories/security/">Security</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Ethereum mainnet, block &lt;code&gt;25816049&lt;/code&gt;. A transaction (&lt;code&gt;0xd354a15b15cb73d30908f411aee3f795ec86737a4d080e9a818ac4d6d3014129&lt;/code&gt;) walks through a proxy contract, calls a function called &lt;code&gt;executeProposal()&lt;/code&gt;, and by the time it&amp;rsquo;s done a wallet that started the day with nothing has &lt;code&gt;2841.743535791961701401&lt;/code&gt; WETH sitting in it. The vault it came from — &lt;code&gt;0x26fCb50eEC367ddAB060ccf5E7394Cecd95F7Db2&lt;/code&gt;, a real Yearn V3 vault with &lt;code&gt;totalAssets()&lt;/code&gt; around 2926 WETH — didn&amp;rsquo;t get hacked in the usual sense. Nobody found a reentrancy bug or a rounding error in a swap. Someone won a vote.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I want to walk through how that vote got won, because the contract that lets you win it is, read in isolation, completely unremarkable.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Fox (FoxLpBondsPool) Attack Analysis: A $482M &#39;Create Your Own Market Then Harvest&#39; Exploit</title>
      <link>https://yinhui1984.github.io/fox-attack-analysis/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 22:11:36 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://yinhui1984.github.io/fox-attack-analysis/</guid>
      <category domain="https://yinhui1984.github.io/categories/security/">Security</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Chain: BSC (56)&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Attack Tx: &lt;code&gt;0x8e1775cbfd44db29744cc6687ff1822d2c47321de6e94062f789ad6181ad5514&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Block: &lt;code&gt;116169049&lt;/code&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;Victim Contracts: &lt;code&gt;FoxLpBondsPool&lt;/code&gt; Proxy &lt;code&gt;0x9fa6D8a13b35E051BFc145918db0111dEc13D1A0&lt;/code&gt; (Implementation &lt;code&gt;0x58E2A853BB14e46BefD3148bd4280370fEA4655A&lt;/code&gt;), &lt;code&gt;Treasury&lt;/code&gt; Proxy &lt;code&gt;0x361d08ff43761E6a7E8Fcabe48048AE9010801cc&lt;/code&gt; (Implementation &lt;code&gt;0x87614d97808dcdecb069fe8489848fa1c001e04d&lt;/code&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Fox is a staking protocol that had been running on BSC for some time, and &lt;code&gt;FoxLpBondsPool&lt;/code&gt; is one of its &amp;ldquo;LP Bond&amp;rdquo; entrypoints: users deposit USDT, the protocol converts half of it into FOX, pairs it with the other half of USDT into PancakeSwap&amp;rsquo;s FOX/USDT pool to get LP tokens, and then records your deposit under a bond-like model—principal is released linearly according to lockup days, plus there&amp;rsquo;s an &amp;ldquo;inviter reward&amp;rdquo;. This incident stemmed from this accounting step, where someone extracted roughly 677.5k USDT in instant profit in a single transaction, plus a massive minting certificate with a paper value close to $500 million that releases slowly over 540 days.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>LaunchpadFactoryAuto drained for $17.7k via arbitrary multicall in Uniswap V4 PositionManager</title>
      <link>https://yinhui1984.github.io/launchpadfactoryauto-attack-analysis/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 11:31:50 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://yinhui1984.github.io/launchpadfactoryauto-attack-analysis/</guid>
      <category domain="https://yinhui1984.github.io/categories/security/">Security</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;On Ethereum block 25692310, &lt;code&gt;LaunchpadFactoryAuto&lt;/code&gt; was exploited for $17,743.91 USDC and 0.0072 WETH (~$17,766 total). The root cause was simple: the permissionless &lt;code&gt;launch()&lt;/code&gt; function passed arbitrary caller-supplied calldata straight to &lt;code&gt;PositionManager.multicall()&lt;/code&gt;. Because the factory owns every liquidity position NFT it deploys, executing calldata under the factory&amp;rsquo;s identity allowed an attacker to grant themselves full operator approvals and burn the liquidity out of every pool.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Transaction: &lt;code&gt;0x9583e95d5c88c7966e269197f4b09022f26b7a27ad2c13660dda6774e3136d14&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>CryptoDAOGlobal Attack Analysic</title>
      <link>https://yinhui1984.github.io/cryptodaoglobal-attack-analysic/</link>
      <pubDate>Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:57:50 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://yinhui1984.github.io/cryptodaoglobal-attack-analysic/</guid>
      <category domain="https://yinhui1984.github.io/categories/security/">Security</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;On BSC block 112652246, this transaction succeeded with 5,206 internal calls. The top-level caller was a contract at 0xf00bC28D22d71Be74Bc8aB0d11Fe77F6D77850ac, invoked by EOA 0x427671b2c8e91034a91fe698f9b7259b2345f45d, and the entry function is literally called &lt;code&gt;attack(address,uint256,uint256)&lt;/code&gt;. When it was over, 13,445.27 USDT had moved to the EOA. This post is about what that transaction did, and how a fork reproduction of it matches the trace to the dollar.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>USM drained for 70.8 ETH by funding 62M FUM against a price that hadn&#39;t been refreshed in 99 days</title>
      <link>https://yinhui1984.github.io/usm-drained-for-70.8-eth-by-funding-62m-fum-against-a-price-that-hadnt-been-refreshed-in-99-days/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2026 21:16:15 +0800</pubDate>
      <guid>https://yinhui1984.github.io/usm-drained-for-70.8-eth-by-funding-62m-fum-against-a-price-that-hadnt-been-refreshed-in-99-days/</guid>
      <category domain="https://yinhui1984.github.io/categories/security/">Security</category>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;On ETH block 25716150, one transaction took 132.59 ETH out of the USM pool and left 61.76. The exploit was a single &lt;code&gt;fund()&lt;/code&gt; call followed by 64 equal-sized &lt;code&gt;defund()&lt;/code&gt; calls, all inside one flash loan. Net profit: 70.830977 ETH. The oracle was never touched.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Transaction: &lt;code&gt;0xfae5e751b8ce01457cbb6b529839f24a0cff50faaabcbd0fd02ca0cf559b050e&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>MetaMask Agent Wallet&#39;s Guard Mode Checks Four Things. The approve() Amount Isn&#39;t One of Them</title>
